<title>NETHERLANDS: Lanschot ups Van Leer to marketperformer.</title>
<headline>Lanschot ups Van Leer to marketperformer.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of April 1 research.</p>
<p>Company-------Sector-----------Price---Broker------------</p>
<p>Van Leer	Basic industries 38.00   Van Lanschot Bankiers</p>
<p>COMMENT: MARKETPERFORMANCE (Underperformance) Van Leer's autonomous sales growth will remain below 4 pct. Therefore, acquisitions preferably at consumer packaging) and further cost cutting are needed to let earnings grow in line with market. Earnings are expected to rise about 15 pct in 1997 instead of 25 pct needed to let earnings grow in line with market. However, for 1998 market EPS growth is seen to be about 12.5 pct, a level which must be attainable for Van Leer.</p>
<p>    Estimates (NLG):  EPS     P/E     P/CF    Dividend</p>
<p>    1996 (actual)     3.22    11.4    4.3     1.00</p>
<p>    1997		  3.45    10.9    4.3     1.15</p>
<p>    1998		  3.90     9.6    4.0     1.30</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
